        "text": "Technical analysis uses previous price and market data to try to identify price patterns and predict future price movements. Unlike fundamental analysis, technical analysis isn't concerned with an asset's underlying or intrinsic value. Instead, technical analysts study price changes, trading volume, chart patterns, technical indicators, and other charting tools to forecast future price moves and trade on these predictions. In short, we can say that technical analysis disregards news and other fundamental factors and is mainly focused on market charts. Technical analysis applies to any financial market and is very popular among cryptocurrency traders. But is it actually effective?",
